{
  "analysis": "Fresh terminal at /app. The user can't curl example.com and wants to know why and how to fix it. I need to diagnose the networking issue step by step.",
  "plan": "Start by attempting the curl and capturing the error. Then diagnose: check DNS resolution, /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts, firewall, proxy env vars, and connectivity. I'll run a series of diagnostic commands.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -v example.com\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "curl fails with 'DNS resolution error'. This points to a DNS configuration problem. I need to inspect the DNS setup: /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts, and whether a resolver like systemd-resolved is running, plus any proxy/DNS overrides.",
  "plan": "Inspect /etc/resolv.conf and /etc/hosts. Try nslookup/host/getent to see if resolution works at all. Check for any unusual config. Then determine the fix.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/resolv.conf\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/hosts\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "getent hosts example.com\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which nslookup host dig 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Interesting clue: `getent hosts example.com` actually resolves successfully (to IPv6 addresses 2606:4700::/...), but curl reports 'DNS resolution error'. The nameserver is 127.0.0.11 (Docker's embedded DNS). The fact that getent works but curl doesn't suggests curl's resolver path behaves differently — possibly it only got IPv6 records, or curl is misconfigured/blocked. I need to dig deeper into the exact failure mode.",
  "plan": "Run targeted diagnostics: try curl with -4 (force IPv4) and -6 (force IPv6) to see if it's an address-family issue; check nsswitch.conf; check for proxy env vars; and test connecting by IP directly to isolate DNS vs connectivity.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/nsswitch.conf 2>/dev/null | grep hosts\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "env | grep -i proxy\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -4 -v example.com\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -6 -v example.com\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

